 <header><div><h1>Veil &middot; simulated assistant</h1>
-<p>A stand-in voice assistant talks to Veil's MCP server (<code>POST /mcp</code>, protocol 2025-11-25). It sees only what the room hears. The right-hand panels are operator instrumentation on a separate token-gated endpoint. Synthetic calendars; no Amazon service or device is involved.</p>
+<p>A stand-in voice assistant talks to Veil's MCP server (<code>POST /mcp</code>, protocol 2025-11-25). It sees only what the room hears. The right-hand panels are operator instrumentation on a separate token-gated endpoint. Synthetic calendars; no Amazon service or device is involved. Hosted demo: each browser's session lives in an encrypted cookie (stateless Vercel functions), not the local server's append-only ledger. Clearing or replaying an older cookie rolls back your own session, and two simultaneous actions may lose one update. Same model and code, different persistence; for trying the mechanism, not a production privacy guarantee.</p>
